  "title": "Samye Monastery",
  "summary": "Samye Monastery in Tibet was established in approximately 775 under the patronage of King Trisong Detsen and is described as the first Buddhist monastery built in Tibet. The Indian abbot Shantarakshita ordained the first seven novice monks in Tibet there, with additional help from Padmasambhava. Another source gives construction dates of 762 to 779.",
